\f0\fs28 \cf2 I need to build a description of the Steel City Codes registration and management system in order to feed it to Claude Code to build an app. Registration begins in late January for both students and volunteers.\
\

\f1\b Volunteer Registration:\

\f0\b0 Administration dispatches volunteers to schools to get students to sign up und fill out the form(VolunteerSignUpForm.txt). In the form, applicants are directed to sign up for an Interview. Administration then conducts these interviews, filling out notes and putting relevant details in the \'93APPLICANT MASTER DOC\'94 workbook in the \'93Volunteers.xlsx\'94. Then, based on information from the form that volunteers filled out and information from the interview, volunteers are grouped into the appropriate classes with the appropriate age groups.(\'93WEEK 1 ASSIGNMENTS\'94, \'93WEEK 2 ASSIGNMENTS\'94) Inexperienced volunteers are matched with experienced volunteers, and based on information from the interviews volunteers are matched with other similar volunteers to make a class. An added layer is that some volunteers don\'92t sign up for both weeks. \
\

\f1\b Student Registration: \

\f0\b0 Administration sends out an email to their mailing list requesting them to sign up for the classes they want based on what to do for each week. Other tertiary information is also collected like allergy info, medical conditions, etc. Students are registered for classes on a first come first serve basis(only a few classes are capped) and then they\'92re grouped into classes based on their age group and parent.\
\

\f1\b Daily Operations:\

\f0\b0 Volunteers have roles during lunch where they\'92re assigned to watch several different areas(Hall Duty, Cafeteria, Playground).\
Volunteers must do attendance every day and ensure that students are in the class rooms.\
Volunteers must log students as they check out of their classes.\
\

\f1\b Ideas for a System:\
\

\f0\b0 We want to create a system where we can manage all student registration and generate classes, manage volunteer registration and interviews and setting them up, and giving them roles. Must be able to do attendance and check out. 
